    "lawCode": "Amd §7-104, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6909A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to party emblems\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe bill repeals the requirement that the party emblem be affixed to\nthe name of each candidate on the ballot.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends Election Law section 7-104, paragraph (a) of\nsubdivision 4, paragraph (c) of subdivision 5, and subdivision 9, to\nremove the requirement that the party emblem appear with the name of\neach candidate on the ballot.\n\nSection 2: Provides for the Act to take effect immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nUnder current law, Section 9-211 requires each county board of\nelections to randomly audit 3% of their voting systems, and the party\nemblem is required to appear in the box with the candidate's name.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe local boards of elections have all observed in performing the\nrequired audit that the presence of the party emblem in the voting box\nmade it much more difficult to accurately perform the audit. The\nmarking area is not very large, and when there is another significant\nmark (the emblem) contained within that area it is tedious to discern\nthe voter's mark from the emblem.\n\nWith the move to the use of paper ballots and optical scan systems,\nthere has also been some confusion among voters with respect to the\nappearance of the party emblem by the candidates name. These emblems\nare not recognized by most voters, and have caused some voters to\nthink that their ballots have already been marked. Since the party of\nthe candidate is clearly marked in the voting box where the\ncandidate's name appears, the use of the party emblem in that box is\nan unnecessary relic that no longer serves any useful purpose, and it\nshould be removed to prevent voter and election administration staff\nconfusion.\n\nThe emblem will remain in the area with the image of a closed fist and\nextended finger and the party or independent name printed on it, which\npoints to the party or independent row with the candidate names.\n\nThis legislation was requested by the State Board of Elections in its\n2010 Election Law Proposals.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
